# Git remote: SSH only

- `origin` must stay `git@github.com:iCodZilla/defhop.git` (SSH).
- Never switch push/fetch URL back to `https://github.com/...` — HTTPS :443 to GitHub often fails on this machine.
- When the user asks to push/pull/create PR remote sync: use `git push` / `git pull` with the existing SSH remote; do not rewrite to HTTPS.
- If SSH auth fails: remind to check `~/.ssh/config` Host `github.com` and that the public key is on GitHub (deploy key or account SSH key).
- Do not change global git config unless the user explicitly asks.
